= Source consolidation =

This page records how major V1 and historical design families are consolidated into the smaller V2 canon. It preserves conceptual provenance without reproducing every superseded meta page.

== Foundations ==
Historical manifesto, welcome, introduction, philosophy, charter, constitution, and foundational-triad material is distilled into:
* [[BITwiki:Principles]]
* [[BITwiki:Governance]]
* [[BITwiki:Content model]]

The durable themes are knowledge compounding, modular memory, ontology/epistemology/axiology, evidence, pluralism, human agency, and revisionability.

== Organization and taxonomy ==
V1 families such as Wiki Organization Guidelines, taxonomy architecture, page types, entity types, domain/schema indexes, portal specifications, organization guidelines, and ontology-alignment documents are consolidated into:
* [[BITwiki:Architecture]]
* [[BITwiki:Organization]]
* [[BITwiki:Classification]]
* [[BITwiki:Schema]]
* [[BITwiki:Navigation]]
* [[BITwiki:Naming conventions]]

== Book Matter and modularity ==
Historical modular-template, section-component, transclusion, literacy, overview/framework/application, and book-matter work is consolidated into:
* [[BITwiki:Book matter]]
* [[BITwiki:Transclusion]]
* [[BITwiki:Content model]]

The preserved idea is semantic content anatomy with selective reuse, not a filesystem of article fragments.

== Evidence and epistemics ==
V1 families including epistemic framework/status/tier pages, evidence framework/evaluation/tier pages, source hierarchy/types, provenance models, uncertainty markers, and epistemic audit material are consolidated into:
* [[BITwiki:Epistemics]]
* [[BITwiki:Provenance]]
* [[BITwiki:Governance]]

== Templates, properties, concepts, modules, and schemas ==
Historical infobox catalogs, template catalogs, property dictionaries, SMW property definitions/types/query references, Lua specifications, dependency/event schemas, and related schema documentation are treated as design evidence for:
* [[BITwiki:Schema]]
* [[BITwiki:Architecture]]
* [[BITwiki:Capability model]]

Actual Template:, Property:, Concept:, Module:, and schema objects should be created only when the V2 implementation needs them.

== Extensions and capability research ==
Historical MediaWiki extension research and experimental plugin inventories are consolidated into:
* [[BITwiki:Capability model]]

Extension availability is not content ontology.

== Audits, revised copies, and deployment-era pages ==
Revision summaries, deployment audits, REVISED/styled variants, duplicate component names, and architecture-about-architecture pages contribute lessons and provenance but do not survive as parallel canonical V2 pages unless their substantive content is unique.

See [[BITwiki:Lessons learned]] and [[BITwiki:Provenance]].

